Adds RIVER_HDR_OUTPUTS, the outputs to drive in HDR: BT.2020 primaries and
the PQ curve at 10 bits, as sway's output hdr does, when the output
advertises both. wlroots then maps SDR content into PQ itself, so those
outputs skip the Display P3 transform, which wlroots would refuse alongside.

HDR is tried on a copy of the modeset's state and only then applied, so an
output that refuses it keeps the format applyRenderFormat chose and gets no
image description: the legacy DRM interface refuses one even when it is
null. An output leaving HDR has its description cleared. The first frame of
a modeset gets the P3 transform too (or, in HDR, none), not unmapped sRGB.

